Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.14), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, gir1.2-pango-1.0
Recommends: imagemagick, gir1.2-gexiv2-0.10, webp-pixbuf-loader, heif-gdk-pixbuf, librsvg2-common,
 libgtk-4-media-gstreamer, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-libav, ffmpeg
Description: simple and fast photo viewer for GNOME
 Argos shows the photos of a folder as a grid of thumbnails, with a folder
 tree on the side, and opens them in a viewer laid out like gThumb: header
 bar, thumbnail strip with an adjustable height, status bar, properties
 (EXIF) panel.
 .
 The mouse wheel goes to the next or previous photo, Ctrl + wheel zooms
 around the pointer, dragging moves a zoomed photo and a double click shows
 it full screen. Neighbouring photos are read in advance.
 .
 Simple editing: rotate, crop and save in another format (ImageMagick).
 Formats are those of GdkPixbuf: JPEG, PNG, GIF (animated), WebP, TIFF,
 BMP, SVG, HEIC and AVIF. It follows the desktop theme.
